:"LIN54","gene_id":"ENSG00000189308","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":true,"nucleus_direction":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":3.08018e-19,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.177319,"nucleus_score":-9.12762,"pct_ad":0.283082,"pct_control":0.315865,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.661251,"donor_log2fc":-0.147622,"donor_lfcse":0.0834333,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-0.0250987}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"Mic","gene_id":"ENSG00000189308","module":"magenta","kme":0.215404,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.939268,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000189308","entrez_id":["132660"],"uniprot":["Q6MZP7"],"ncbi_summary":"LIN54 is a component of the LIN, or DREAM, complex, an essential regulator of cell cycle genes (Schmit et al., 2009 [PubMed 19725879]).[supplied by OMIM, Dec 2010].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q6MZP7","text":"Component of the DREAM complex, a multiprotein complex that can both act as a transcription activator or repressor depending on the context (PubMed:17531812, PubMed:17671431). In G0 phase, the complex binds to more than 800 promoters and is required for repression of E2F target genes (PubMed:17531812, PubMed:17671431). In S phase, the complex selectively binds to the promoters of G2/M genes whose products are required for mitosis and participates in their cell cycle dependent activation (PubMed:17531812, PubMed:17671431). In the complex, acts as a DNA-binding protein that binds the promoter of CDK1 in a sequence-specific manner (PubMed:19725879). Specifically recognizes the consensus motif 5'-TTYRAA-3' in target DNA (PubMed:27465258)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}